      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a somewhat weird case; the normal check for higher priority is to have a lower prio value; this will automatically include RT prios, since those are mapped at [0..99] vs the nice values at [100..140].\n\nBut, if both threads have the same prio, and one thread is SCHED_FIFO and the other is SCHED_RR, which do you consider the higher prio? Since SCHED_FIFO can run unbounded and SCHED_RR can\u0027t, SCHED_FIFO is considered higher here. I\u0027ll add a comment to clarify.",
